<https://example.org/dmo/id/contraindication/diabetic-ketoacidosis-dka> a dmo:Contraindication ;
    rdfs:label "Diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA)" ;
    dmo:contraCode "diabetic-ketoacidosis-dka" ;
    dmo:rationale "High levels of ketones in your blood can lead to a condition called diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA) External link. DKA is a medical emergency that should be treated right away. DKA is most common in people with type 1 diabetes. Occasionally, DKA may affect people with type 2 diabetes who have lost their ability to produce insulin." ;
    dmo:severity "Absolute" ;
    dmo:triggerCriteria "If your body does not have enough insulin, it can’t use glucose as a source of energy and will use fat instead. When your body uses fat for energy, your body makes chemicals called ketones." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "High levels of ketones in your blood can lead to a condition called diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA) External link. DKA is a medical emergency that should be treated right away." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-healthy-living-with-diabetes> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/contraindication/low-blood-glucose> a dmo:Contraindication ;
    rdfs:label "Low blood glucose" ;
    dmo:contraCode "low-blood-glucose" ;
    dmo:rationale "Physical activity often lowers the level of glucose in your blood. Low blood glucose levels may last for hours or days after physical activity. Low blood glucose can be a serious medical emergency that must be treated right away." ;
    dmo:severity "Absolute" ;
    dmo:triggerCriteria "You are most likely to have low blood glucose if you take insulin or some other diabetes medicines, such as sulfonylureas." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "You are most likely to have low blood glucose if you take insulin or some other diabetes medicines, such as sulfonylureas." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-healthy-living-with-diabetes> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/contraindication/physical-activities-that-need-balance> a dmo:Contraindication ;
    rdfs:label "Physical activities that need balance" ;
    dmo:contraCode "physical-activities-that-need-balance" ;
    dmo:rationale "Some activities that need balance may be unsafe for people with nerve damage or vision problems caused by diabetes." ;
