<https://example.org/dmo/id/contraindication/taking-less-insulin-before-physical-activity> a dmo:Contraindication ;
    rdfs:label "Taking less insulin before physical activity" ;
    dmo:contraCode "taking-less-insulin-before-physical-activity" ;
    dmo:rationale "Taking less insulin before physical activity may help prevent low blood glucose, but it may also make you more likely to have high blood glucose. If your body does not have enough insulin, it can’t use glucose as a source of energy and will use fat instead. When your body uses fat for energy, your body makes chemicals called ketones." ;
    dmo:severity "Relative" ;
    dmo:triggerCriteria "Taking less insulin before physical activity may help prevent low blood glucose, but it may also make you more likely to have high blood glucose." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Taking less insulin before physical activity may help prevent low blood glucose, but it may also make you more likely to have high blood glucose." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-healthy-living-with-diabetes> .

